;; spec:   stdlib §2.3 (KeyReducible: Map and Vec), §4.4 row reduce-kv, §5 T (a static-typing fact)
;; expect: reject
;; error:  no implementation of KeyReducible for (List i64)
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: reduce-kv
;; Only a keyed collection has keys: Clojure's (reduce-kv f 0 '(1 2)) throws at run time, and here the program is rejected
;; at compile time, naming the type that has no KeyReducible instance. The instances are Map (key and value) and Vec (index
;; and element), and a program's own type adds one (case 2584).
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq fib.coll))

(defun main () -> i64
  (reduce-kv (fn (a k v) (+ a v)) 0 (list 1 2)))
